  "description": "Manual rework request: agent:rework label on the PR itself -> rework on demand, ANY author (owner override: a manual label by a write/admin actor fires even on guest PRs). PR-anchored (gh-683 bug E, live fa #1194 2026-10-04: the {issueNumber} body-scrape resolved a stale bare '#327' mention — a wrong-but-EXISTING issue, so the #544 existence guard passed it — while the real linked issue was gh-1044; the factory guard rejected the anchor, run=false, 75s no-op, and the failed consume (bug D) re-fanned it every tick). The label is ON the PR and the rework runs on the PR head, so anchor on inputs.pr directly (the same PR-anchored shape as review-on-label / review-external-once / review-machine-unlinked): preCliReworkSetup's #544 path runs the leg on pr-<N> with no ticket lookup, no scrape, no anchor to mis-resolve. The PR label is consumed on dispatch so the next tick does not re-fire. gh-715: the engine's cross-anchor guard (smAgent triggerWorkflow) also consumes the label when the dispatch is SUPPRESSED because a leg for the same issue/PR is already in flight under the other anchor (e.g. an issue-anchored rework run while this PR-anchored rule matched) — the active run fulfills the request, and consuming prevents a duplicate leg on the next quiet tick; rework-unresolved-threads re-arms the PR if the threads stay unresolved, so the recovery path is intact. workflowRef={branch}: the leg runs on the PR head.",
